el that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.","Saying a choice is good without naming the actual detail does not show understanding.","Copy the model word-for-word and call that independent work.","Treat a missing detail as a stated fact."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Explain the evidence\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific error, then show how a revision fixes that error. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific error, then show how a revision fixes that error.","A superficial change in length or appearance does not repair meaning. A decorative picture without a useful label or caption is not evidence for a numerical claim.","Treat a missing detail as a stated fact.","Skip the prompt because the first idea sounded good."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Test a misconception\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use the method on a new topic, not a reworded copy of the example. Review the result for accuracy and reader clarity. The other choices avoid explaining the actual strategy.","options":["Use the method on a new topic, not a reworded copy of the example. Review the result for accuracy and reader clarity.","Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new content.","Skip the prompt because the first idea sounded good.","Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event."],"question":"Which idea is taught in the stage \"Transfer to an independent example\"?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"A bar graph clearly compares quantities across garde