r trying \"Describe why the warned-against approach would weaken your work, then write a co\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The new example should meet the same purpose as the model, but contain original material. Useful feedback uses the original evidence or language point.","options":["The new example should meet the same purpose as the model, but contain original material.","Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new content.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Make one fresh example demonstrating the skill and explain your main choice.\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence, not repetition of the worked model, demonstrates the skill.","marking_guide":"Require independently produced relevant work with accurate reasoning and a specific supporting detail.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating the central skill, explaining the particular words or evidence that make it work.","sample_answer":"Original demonstration: A labelled frog-life-cycle diagram shows stages and arrows; a bar graph compares frog sightings by month; a caption such as ''Tadpoles develop legs before becoming froglets'' interprets a stage without repeating a vague title.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A correction needs to change meaning or accuracy, not just make the text longer.","marking_guide":"Require an actual misconception plus corrected example and purpose-linked explanation.","question":"Name one likely error in using this skill, correct it and explain why the correction helps.","sample_answer":"Common error: A decorative picture without a useful label or caption is not evidence for a numerical claim. Correction: A bar graph clearly compares quantities across gardens. A labelled drawing may identify body parts but does not display the counts as effectively.","type"